version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-voice
description: >-
  Kernel voice: the supervised voice child (voice-child.ts, voice-control.ts,
  voice-install.ts), enrolment, voice requests, and the stores for reply mode,
  input choice and the send word.
context:
  - >-
    The send flows $send-by-word and $send-by-pieces stay in
    packages/gnomon/.purpose; the darwin audio binary is packages/gnomon-voice.
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  gnomon-voice:
    description: >-
      TD-2026-10-23-496 (supersedes G-VOX-06 on the send-word path only):
      under a send-word or pieces ceiling (liability acknowledged on the
      start row) the held word from the attached human's voice principal
      counts whoever said it (wordAnyVoice: isWord, speakerEnrolled false,
      speakerVerified false, never a draft part) and a word claim is accepted
      over unverified or inherited draft turns; the send is stamped
      voice-unverified (originFor: the consumed word came from any voice, or
      the draft holds an unverified or inherited turn). Pieces, send-now,
      Talk and the direct send keep the gate; intercepted turns are refused.
      Aegis review 2026-10-23 (H-1, M-1, M-2, L-1..L-3): an inherited
      (continuity) turn is NOT verification (UserTurn.basis 'continuity'):
      every send that includes one is stamped voice-unverified (originFor,
      attributed or a voice-hinted edit), it never anchors adjacency, the
      voice principal never sends it directly (cause 'inherited'), and a
      piece claim must cite a turn verified alone (cause 'inherited-only').
      Inheritance is capped per anchor (VOICE_CONTINUITY_MAX_TURNS 2,
      VOICE_CONTINUITY_MAX_MS of t1 - t0), the clip is at most
      VOICE_CONTINUITY_CLIP_MS long, the gap and the stretch are also
      checked on kernel receipt times (+ VOICE_CONTINUITY_RECEIPT_SLACK_MS,
      anchorReceivedAt), t0 may not precede the previous t1 (50 ms grace), a voice.bargein row or
      or model streaming since the previous turn breaks it. The send word never
      rides continuity. Talk (narrow): a ptt clip with gated speech under the
      minimum that is not verified is draftOnly (a long one keeps the gate).
      status.voice.mic level and inputs reach the human class on the gui
      credential only (voiceStatusFor); request.voice.client{op:'mic-meter',
      open} sets status.voice.micMeterOpen (lapses after
      VOICE_MIC_METER_TTL_MS) and the voice app relays the level only then.
      appendCappedLog re-applies 0700/0600 on every write.
      2026-10-23 (founder field bugs): speaker CONTINUITY at receipt
      (#continuityOf; contracts VOICE_CONTINUITY_GAP_MS 3 s,
      VOICE_CONTINUITY_STRETCH_MS 30 s): a voice.turn.user{speakerBasis:
      'continuity'} with gatedSpeechMs under VOICE_MIN_VERIFY_SPEECH_MS is
      its speaker's only when the turn right before it on the attachment is
      an accepted turn of that speaker on the same connection (verified alone
      or by continuity: UserTurn.anchorT1), within the gap, inside the
      stretch of the last turn verified alone, with no agent playback between
      and not intercepted; else it is unverified. A short send word needs
      adjacency whatever basis it claims. Dictate's draft-only exception now
      covers every send ceiling of a conversation attachment (short speech is
      never thrown away; word, pieces and send-now stay refused while it is
      in the draft). request.voice.report{mic} (MicReport: device, aec,
      fault, on, inputs, selected, missing, level; a state per connection)
      is status.voice.mic; request.voice.client{op:'select-input', id, name?}
      (human, gui or device) sets status.voice.inputChoice, persisted at
      <home>/voice/input.json (input-choice-store.ts, 0600). The held send
      word lives in <home>/voice/send-word.json (send-word-store.ts, 0600,
      atomic temp-and-rename, read through a stat-keyed cache; the stored word
      is #send-word-matcher canonicalSendWord, and a file that does not parse
      holds no word), written by request.voice.sendword and `gnomon voice
      send-word set|clear` alike. The voice child's
      stderr is appended to <home>/logs/voice.log (0600, rolls to voice.log.1
      past 256 KiB) besides the 2000-char lastError tail.
      Dictate, the G-VOX-06 exception (founder bug 2026-10-21): under a
      conversation ceiling with send ceiling key, an unverified speaker's
      ambient, non-intercepted turn of the attached human's voice principal is
      not refused voice-speaker at receipt; the other guards run and an
      accepted one is stamped forwardable, draftOnly:true and
      speakerVerified:false (client claims of either are BAD_REQUEST). Aegis
      privacy: its row is HASH-ONLY; its words stay in kernel memory
      (UNVERIFIED_TEXT_TTL_MS, UNVERIFIED_TEXT_CAP) and reach only a human on
      the gui credential, for sessions that human owns now:
      VoiceControl.unverifiedFor(principal), added per viewer by the
      dispatcher as status.voice.unverified (status() never carries them;
      voiceStatusFor strips them for any other class or credential). It fills the draft only: the direct send is refused, and a
      word, piece or send-now claim on that session is refused
      voice-speaker{cause draft-only} while ANY attachment's unverified turn
      there is unsent (a preset switch re-attaches); it is never the send
      word nor an adjacency anchor; only a human session.send (Enter) carries
      it, and originFor stamps that send sentBy 'unverified' (turn.sent
      origin voice-unverified, a record only, #voice-origin) when its
      attribution matched one or a source:'voice' send happens while one is
      outstanding (consumed; releaseOrigin hands them back on a failed send). A refused unverified turn under
      VOICE_MIN_VERIFY_SPEECH_MS (contracts) of gated speech carries cause
      too-short.
      Voice drops fix (2026-10-20): busy (voice-playback) ends at the main-chain
      end_turn message_stop (supervisor turnBusy), re-armed by message_start;
      the append result carries refused/refusedCause; capture reports carry
      refusal/cause; voice.turn.user keeps speakerScore (bucket) and
      gatedSpeechMs; the kernel stamps localDrops counts (VoiceReports
      takeLocalDrops) on voice.turn.user and voice.session.end.
      Aegis M2: every enrolments.jsonl write (CLI enrol/forget, card enrol) goes
      through appendSignedEnrolRow (sig verified, seq recomputed under the
      lock, moved seq refused loudly, durable append). A missing `consent` is
      never "unconsented"; the text lives in voice/consents/<hex>.txt.
      TD-2026-10-20-514 (Aegis Q3/F3): the GUI enrol card is ROOT class and
      hand-only; prepareEnrol builds the voiceEnrolRow:v1 row (+cardId,
      consentHash; seq under the enrolments lock), commitEnrol re-checks seq
      and writes the consent text to voice/consents/<hex>.txt; the consent
      never enters the card or the log. ONE presence.
      Dictation (TD-2026-10-20-262): accepted voice.turn.user rows carry a
      kernel-stamped forwardable (a client forwardable is BAD_REQUEST); a human
      session.send{source:'voice'} is hash-matched against the attachment's
      pending turns and tagged turn.sent{source voice|voice-edited, voiceSessionId,
      voiceTurnSeqs, voiceTurnSeq} (attribution never refuses); request.voice.report
      {dictation} is relayed as status.voice.dictation{activity, holdToggles, at}.
      #gnomon-voice kernel side, slices V1 talk-only and V2a ambient (TD-2026-10-19-298:
      the attachment mode is a ceiling, ptt under any, conversation only under
      conversation; widening to conversation takes one fresh-presence strictness
      card per GUI login; ambient turns need an aec claim, an enrolled speaker and
      a not-busy session by the supervisor's own turn state plus the echo tail
      (voice-playback, clock kernel); idle auto-off of a conversation ceiling after
      voice.ambientIdleMs, default ten minutes, written voice.session.end reason idle;
      receipt-refused and unknown-speaker turns are stored as a keyed text hash,
      duration and reason, never text; status.voice attached, hsid, ceiling, since,
      idleAt) (spec §14.1-14.4, §14.7
      Forwarding guards and No level, run modes; §4.10; T-2026-10-19-026,
      TD-2026-10-19-194, TD-2026-10-19-677). src/kernel/voice/voice-control.ts:
      attachment ONLY by a human gesture (log.append voice.session.start|end on a
      first-party GUI/device connection; the kernel mints voiceSessionId and
      writes the row); voice session.send to the attached session only, source
      voice forced, riding the attaching human's turn permit (never its own),
      accepted only for the voice connection's latest voice.turn.user in this
      attachment from an enrolled speaker, not intercepted, push-to-talk, outside
      every voice.turn.agent playback window + echoTailMs (750). Refusals are
      FORBIDDEN gate voice with reserved reasons: voice-target, voice-conn,
      voice-stale-utterance, voice-speaker, voice-grammar, voice-echo, voice-off
      (conversation mode). session.stop interrupt only; voice.* shape-validated;
      the voice reader sees its attached session + voice.*, redacted. approve stays
      voice-off in every form; request.voice.arm stays refused (V7).
      src/kernel/voice/enrolment.ts + src/cli/voice-cli.ts: gnomon voice setup |
      enrol | forget, root-signed rows (enrolments.jsonl, voice device key).
      Aegis V1 conditions: kernel receipt time stamped on voice.turn.user|agent
      (receivedAt); a turn is forwardable for VOICE_TURN_MAX_AGE_MS (30 s) after
      receipt, never before the attachment, echo checked on kernel times too;
      per-turn client mode claim cross-checked against the attachment (ptt is a
      client claim, §A.4); voice follow subscriptions end on every attachment
      change (SubscriptionHub.endReaderClass); turn.sent / session.inject carry
      source voice + voiceSessionId, turnId, voiceTurnSeq (the link); the voice
      reader sees only its attached session's rows; enrolment order is the
      signed seq; windows bounded at VOICE_WINDOW_CAP.
      Slice V2e (spec §14.4.1): src/kernel/voice/voice-child.ts VoiceChildSupervisor
      spawns the voice client over an inherited socketpair (fd 3) the kernel
      authenticates itself as p:<ns>/voice (SocketServerHandle.adopt +
      dispatcher.adoptPreauthenticated, no hello/auth, no key in the child),
      allow-list env, backoff restarts, dies on every daemon exit and drain
      (TD-908). voice-install.ts copies + codesign-verifies GnomonVoiceIO.app
      into <home>/bin/voice and fetches models; T-2026-10-21-028
      (#release-pins): the copied executable is hashed before and after
      codesign (VOICE_IO_REQUIREMENT from gnomon-contracts, the build's own),
      must equal the release's compiled sha256 for this arch in a release
      build (VoiceAppRefused 'checksum', dev flag or not) and answer
      --version ≥ MIN_VOICE_IO_VERSION in every build ('version');
      createVoicePrepare re-verifies it LAST, right before the spawn
      (recheckVoiceApp: path, inode, size, mtime, sha256, the release pin,
      codesign hash-verify-rehash), so the model-fetch window cannot swap it; the client entry resolves
      lazily, darwin only. Aegis M2: at DAEMON START createVoicePrepare checks
      the workspace gnomon-voice dist against dist/voice-client.manifest.json
      and that manifest against the loaded build stamp's voiceClientManifest
      (scripts/build-stamp.mjs; build gnomon-voice first), then copies all of
      dist, voice-models.manifest.json, a module package.json and the optional
      sherpa-onnx-node + platform packages into <home>/bin/voice/client
      (0700/0600), pins a
      sha256 of every file in memory, runs the model fetch and the spawn from
      the COPY, and re-verifies the pin last in every prepare; a changed,
      added or missing file is VoiceClientRefused, phase 'unavailable' with
      the reason, never retried. Every exit (signal, stop, idle, upgrade after
      its drain) goes through shutdown(), which awaits voiceChild.close(). voice-requests.ts: dispatcher-only request.voice.enrol
      (fresh-presence strictness card, detail.op voice.enrol, writes the
      root-signed row), request.voice.forget (no card), request.voice.report
      (client progress + notices relayed in status.voice; 2026-10-20
      prints{stale: names} = speakers whose print predates the client's
      speech gate, held per voice connection with no TTL, cleared when it
      closes, relayed as status.voice.prints; T-2026-10-20-005
      A1 capture{state idle|hearing|transcribing|captured|dropped, segId,
      reason? closed too-short|echo|not-attached|no-words|not-enrolled|
      barge-in|refused on dropped only, level? 0..1 on hearing only} relayed
      as status.voice.capture with VOICE_CAPTURE_TTL_MS 5 s; voiceStatusFor
      projects B1's capture.text{committed, tail} (the live partial words,
      hearing / transcribing only, voice principal only, sanitised, capped
      at CAPTURE_TEXT_MAX 600, in memory with the capture TTL, never a row)
      to a human-class connection on the gui credential only (V2; the shared
      CAPTURE_STATUS_KEYS never include text); voice.capture.level declared in status-numbers.ts. Aegis
      follow-ups: terminal states are marked claim:'client' and cross-checked
      against the kernel's own acceptances on that voice connection
      (VoiceControl onAccepted turn|send, 5 s window): a contradicted drop
      shows captured with kernel:'accepted' and clientReason, a captured with
      no acceptance is kernel:'unconfirmed'; text only for cls human on the
      gui credential; the slot remembers its connId and clears when that
      connection closes); request.voice.client
      start|stop is human only. speakable.ts KernelSpeakable appends
      voice.turn.agent{source kernel-speakable, turnSeq, items} for the attached
      session; the voice reader is narrowed to voice.* rows. speakerEnrolled is
      the kernel's call (readEnrolled). No §9.1 kind added; clientApiId unchanged.
      TABLE TALK (TD-2026-10-20-294, docs/guides/table-talk.md): the reply item
      prefers the first speak fenced block (markdown, URLs and long digit/hex runs
      stripped, 300-char sentence cap, unclosed fence = its first paragraph)
      as from:'block', else the gnome line / first paragraph as from:'heuristic';
      kernel-written ask-waiting and edits items carry from:'kernel'.
      table-talk.ts holds the frozen guidance (at most 160 words, pinned hash);
      VoiceControl.guidanceFor(hsid) returns it only while voice is attached
      to that session, and the #supervisor writes it as a second
      <gnomon-voice> text block on every send (turn.sent guidanceHash;
      contentHash stays the human text, replay unchanged). The spoken scrub
      (scrubSpoken) also covers heuristic and ask items (Aegis L2); gnomon
      trace allows one extra prompt block only when turn.sent names its
      guidanceHash and the hash matches (Aegis M2).
    path: src/kernel/voice/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, voice, paradigm-8, move-4]
    flows: [$voice-turn]
    tests:
      - test/voice-v1.test.ts
      - test/voice-v2e.test.ts
      - test/voice-v2e-daemon.test.ts
      - test/voice-v2e-enrol.test.ts
      - test/voice-v2e-speak.test.ts
      - test/table-talk.test.ts
      - test/table-talk-session.test.ts
      - test/voice-enrolment.test.ts
      - test/voice-golden.test.ts
      - test/socket-abi.test.ts
      - test/socket-log-read.test.ts
    oracles: [G-VOX-04, G-VOX-06]
  voice-reply-mode:
    description: >-
      #voice-reply-mode (founder request 2026-10-23, "just type back and not
      speak"; spec §14.4.1; src/kernel/voice/reply-mode-store.ts).
      Speak and show ('speak', the default) or Show only ('show'). The human
      sets it with request.voice.client{op:'reply-mode', mode} on a gui or
      device connection (dispatcher, human only, no card: it only narrows
      what the voice app does); VoiceReports holds it, status.voice.replyMode
      reports it, and the daemon persists it per kernel home at
      <home>/voice/reply.json (0600 in 0700, atomic; a missing or malformed
      file reads as speak) and restores it at start. The kernel's speakable
      projection, turn guidance and the GUI's arrangement are unchanged; the
      voice app (gnomon-voice VoiceClient#checkReplyMode) plays no
      kernel-speakable row under show and stops a reply being said when it
      turns on. Voice input stays as it is.
    path: src/kernel/voice/reply-mode-store.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, voice]
    tests:
      - test/voice-v2e-speak.test.ts
      - test/voice-v2e.test.ts
    oracles: [G-VOX-22]
